  Sources, versions and the changes made:
    - 1995 Street Tree Census, Department of Parks and Recreation, dataset kyad-zm4j (last updated 4 October 2017).
      https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/kyad-zm4j
    - 2005 Street Tree Census, Department of Parks and Recreation, dataset 29bw-z7pj (last updated 10 October 2017).
      https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/29bw-z7pj
    - 2015 Street Tree Census - Tree Data, Department of Parks and Recreation, dataset uvpi-gqnh (last updated
      4 October 2017).
      https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/uvpi-gqnh
      Changes to all three: dead trees, stumps, shafts and planting spaces left out; each tree placed by its own
      latitude and longitude into a 2010 Neighborhood Tabulation Area (or, where the census could not place it, the
      area the census itself named); species names written one way for all three censuses.
    - 2010 Census Tracts, Department of City Planning, dataset bmjq-373p.
      https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/bmjq-373p
      Changes: the tracts dissolved into their 2010 Neighborhood Tabulation Areas (the NTA code each tract carries);
      park, cemetery and airport areas left out of the map; outlines simplified by about 1.5 m.
    Nothing here implies endorsement by the City of New York or any of its agencies.

